 "text": "He left the city a 200-year bet. Guess how it ended? 1790, a thousand pounds, about $4,500, goes into the chest. His rule, lend it to young tradesmen at 5% and keep lending the interest. He did the math himself. One hundred years, \u00a3131,000. Two hundred years, over four million. 1890, the chest opens, $391,000. Only two-thirds of his math. The man who made the bet, Ben Franklin. Part of it builds a trade school. The rest goes back in the chest. 1990, the chest opens again, almost five million dollars. Less than a third of what his math promised. Fewer tradesmen borrowed, many didn't pay back, and the money got parked in safe, slow accounts. The math never failed. People interrupted it. So could you leave your money alone for twenty years? Yes or no?",
